            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "The climate of these two regions differs strongly between a dry, Mediterranean climate in IP and a moderate, strongly topographically influenced climate in NAL. The IP region is ~6.5 times larger compared to NAL (ca. 1000 000 km\u00b2 vs. ca. 150 000 km\u00b2), with a moderate supercell occurrence (1420 mesocyclones and 20.8% LMs.) The NAL is a comparatively smaller region, however, it has a higher supercell occurrence for its area with 447 detected mesocyclones in the current climate and a LM-ratio of 11.6%.",
